# Only what the image build needs is sent to Docker.
.git
.github
**/node_modules
client/dist
**/.vite
docs
deploy/compose/secrets
deploy/compose/smoke.*
deploy/compose/.env
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
.env
# Local data and build output. None of it is in the images, and the
# server stage copies the whole context, so it would land in that
# stage's layers and the build cache (security review L25):
#   - data holds the owner's client files, such as data/kro/client.
#   - dist is the output of scripts/release.sh.
#   - generated is local generated output.
# These patterns name the top-level folders only. Packages embed their
# own data folders, such as server/economy/core/data.
data
dist
generated
bin
backups
# Backups, keys and environment files anywhere in the tree.
**/*.age
**/*.dump
**/secrets
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/.env*
